# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Your data. NEXTRON keeps everything under ~/.config/nextron, never in the
# repository -- but these patterns are here so that a stray copy, a symlink or
# a hasty `git add -A` can never publish a credential or a server address.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
Sources
Sources/
*.ovpn
*.wgconf
*.conf
!.vscode/*.conf
credentials*
*auth*.txt
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.p12
*.log
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.env
.env.*

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Working documents: notes, not code. Nothing here is needed to run NEXTRON.
# Delete this line if you would rather publish the design spec as well.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
nextron.md

# Editor / OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
